```ADD_PAPER
2508.13070v1
Reinforced Context Order Recovery (ReCOR) proposes a reinforcement-learning framework to dynamically determine token generation orders for masked diffusion models. By self-supervising on token prediction difficulty, ReCOR estimates the “hardness” of generating each unfilled token and adaptively selects the next token during both training and inference. This flexible token ordering is particularly beneficial for reasoning and planning tasks, including logic puzzles, where conventional fixed (left-to-right) or random orders fall short. Extensive experiments on challenging benchmarks demonstrate that ReCOR significantly boosts performance—often surpassing baselines and even oracle models defined by the ground-truth token order. Notably, it achieves higher accuracy and improved inference efficiency compared to autoregressive models, marking a promising advance in adaptive diffusion-based generation.
```ADD_PAPER
``` 
~~~~~~~~~~~
