```ADD_PAPER
2502.06768v3
"Train for the Worst, Plan for the Best" rigorously investigates the dichotomy between masked diffusion models (MDMs) and autoregressive models (ARMs) with a focus on adaptive token-ordering strategies. The paper examines how MDMs, which must solve an exponentially large set of infill problems during training, can be made more effective at inference by dynamically selecting the next token based on its predicted difficulty. This adaptive ordering mechanism is shown to notably boost performance on both text generation and logic puzzles—improving reasoning tasks (e.g., elevating Sudoku accuracy from below 7% to roughly 90%) and achieving higher text likelihood and better perplexity metrics than standard ARMs. Extensive experiments demonstrate that by smartly reordering token predictions, the system effectively bypasses hard subproblems, delivering superior accuracy and efficiency across diverse benchmarks.
```ADD_PAPER
``` 
~~~~~~~~~~~
