```ADD_PAPER
2502.03540v4
Path Planning for Masked Diffusion Model Sampling introduces a two-stage inference mechanism that splits the generation process into a planning phase and a denoising phase. In the planning phase, the model dynamically selects which tokens to update next, effectively adapting the generation order based on predictive difficulties. This adaptive strategy is shown to mitigate hard-to-predict subproblems, which can be crucial when tackling tasks like logic puzzles and complex text generation. The method not only improves the overall generation accuracy and likelihood but also demonstrates substantial efficiency gains over traditional autoregressive models. Comprehensive experiments across logic-puzzle benchmarks and text generation tasks validate that this planning-based approach leads to notable improvements in both inference performance and solution quality.
``` 
~~~~~~~~~~~
