```ADD_PAPER
2507.12345v1
We present a new adaptive token-ordering strategy tailored for masked diffusion models (MDMs) that dynamically selects tokens for denoising based on a learned difficulty score. Unlike traditional autoregressive models (ARMs) that follow a fixed left-to-right ordering, our method rearranges the token prediction sequence to first resolve the easiest elements, thereby reducing error propagation and avoiding hard subproblems. Extensive experiments show that on text generation and logic-puzzle benchmarks, our approach not only improves overall likelihood scores but also raises puzzle-solving accuracy by up to 20% compared to leading ARMs. Detailed ablation studies reveal that the adaptive ordering leads to a more balanced error distribution and significantly faster convergence during inference. This work underscores the potential of order-adaptive inference to achieve superior accuracy and efficiency in diffusion-based generative tasks.
```ADD_PAPER
``` 
~~~~~~~~~~~
