```ADD_PAPER
2505.10446v2
"Reinforcing the Diffusion Chain of Lateral Thought with Diffusion Language Models" presents a novel reinforcement learning framework that redefines token generation in diffusion language models. Rather than adhering to a fixed, left-to-right order, the method treats each intermediate denoising step as a latent “thinking” action. It optimizes the overall reasoning trajectory by assigning rewards based on the correctness of the final output, which in turn informs the adaptive selection of token orders. This non-linear, flexible token sequencing greatly mitigates error buildup and enhances the model’s capacity to tackle challenging logic puzzles and text reasoning benchmarks. Extensive experiments on math, code, and reasoning tasks demonstrate that this adaptive strategy significantly improves both likelihood and accuracy compared to conventional autoregressive methods.
```ADD_PAPER
